==============================================================================
 SLICE 2C - COUNTING CODE LINES, COMMENT LINES, BLANK LINES
==============================================================================

Three numbers per file (Blueprint 9.3):

  ncloc         lines with REAL CODE ("non-comment lines of code")
  commentLines  lines that contain a comment
  blankLines    lines with nothing, or only spaces/tabs

They can OVERLAP, so they do not always add up to the total:

  7   String url = "http://example.com"; // a comment
      -> code AND comment. Counted once in ncloc, once in commentLines.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 BIG IDEA - WHY TOKENS, NOT TEXT SEARCH
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Text search for "//" would think this line has a comment:
    String url = "http://example.com";
But "http://example.com" is ONE token: a LITERAL (a string).
The "//" is inside it, so it is NOT a comment.

JavaParser labels every token with a category:
    KEYWORD     class, int, return
    IDENTIFIER  url, Mixed, count
    LITERAL     "http://...", 1, a text block
    SEPARATOR   { } ( ) ;
    OPERATOR    = + &&
    COMMENT     // ... , /* ... */ , /** ... */
    WHITESPACE / EOL   spaces and line breaks (ignored)

Each token knows its begin line and end line. So:
    ncloc        = number of DIFFERENT lines touched by code tokens
    commentLines = number of DIFFERENT lines touched by comment tokens

"DIFFERENT lines" -> we put line numbers into a Set.
A Set ignores duplicates (Phase 0 lesson!), so a line with 5 tokens
is still counted once.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 THE FIXTURE, LINE BY LINE (Mixed.java)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

   1 package fixtures.lines;                 code
   2                                         blank
   3 /**                                     comment
   4  * Javadoc is a comment.                comment
   5  */                                     comment
   6 class Mixed {                           code
   7     String url = "http://..."; // ...   code + comment
   8     /* block comment                    comment
   9                                         comment + blank
  10        still the comment */ int ...     comment + code
  11                                         blank
  12     String text = """                   code
  13         first                           code (inside text block)
  14                                         code + blank
  15         """;                            code
  16 }                                       code

  ncloc 9, comment 7, blank 4

Surprises to remember:
  - Line 9 is empty but INSIDE a /* */ comment: comment AND blank.
  - Line 14 is empty but INSIDE a text block: code AND blank.
    (a text block is one LITERAL token covering lines 12-15)
  - Blank is measured on the plain text; the Blueprint says blank
    lines are "separate from token metrics".

