==============================================================================
 SLICE 2D - COUNTING TODO AND FIXME
==============================================================================

What it does:
  Counts the words TODO and FIXME, but ONLY inside comments.
  Programmers write these as notes: "this still needs work".

Three rules (Blueprint 9.3):
  1. Only inside comments.
       // TODO fix           -> counts
       String s = "TODO";    -> does NOT count (it is a string)
       int FIXME = 1;        -> does NOT count (it is a variable name)
  2. Whole word, any upper/lower case.
       TODO  todo  Todo  TODO:  (todo)  @todo   -> count
       TODOs  TODO_LATER  xTODO  FIX ME         -> do NOT count
  3. Count every time it appears, not lines.
       // TODO TODO todo    -> 3

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 NEW IDEA - A TWO-STEP SEARCH (tokens first, then regex)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Step 1: tokens find the comments (same as Slice 2C). Strings and
        variable names are never even looked at.
Step 2: inside ONE comment's text, a regular expression (regex) finds
        the word.

Regex is a mini-language for text patterns:
    \bTODO\b    with CASE_INSENSITIVE
    \b = "word boundary" = the edge of a word.
          "TODO:" -> after O comes ":" -> edge -> match
          "TODOs" -> after O comes "s" -> no edge -> no match
          "_" counts as a word letter, so "TODO_LATER" does not match.

Why is regex OK here but NOT for finding methods?
  Inside one comment, a word is just a word. But Java structure
  (methods, classes) has nesting, generics, strings, comments...
  A regex gets fooled. That is why we use the parser for structure.

Pattern.compile(...) is done ONCE and stored in a static final field.
A Pattern never changes (immutable), so it is safe to reuse.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 MUTATION CHECKS (real run)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Removed \b            -> "TODOs TODO_LATER xTODO" gave todo 3 (should be 0)
                          test partOfALongerWordDoesNotCount failed
  Searched ALL tokens   -> "TODO" string and FIXME variable were counted
                          test markersOutsideCommentsAreIgnored failed
  Restored              -> 58/58 pass
  Each rule has its own guard test.

