==============================================================================
 SLICE 2E - ONE RECORD PER METHOD
==============================================================================

What it does:
  For every method and constructor, one MethodMeasurement:
    ownerLabel       which class it belongs to
    signature        name + parameter types, e.g. price(int, int)
    declarationKind  METHOD / CONSTRUCTOR / COMPACT_CONSTRUCTOR
    hasBody          false for abstract methods
    beginLine, endLine
    ncloc            code lines inside the method
  (the field names come straight from the database schema and API)

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 BIG IDEA 1 - IDENTITY: HOW DO WE TELL TWO METHODS APART?
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    int price(int units)                 -> price(int)
    int price(int units, int discount)   -> price(int, int)
Same NAME, different PARAMETERS = "overloads". If we used only the
name, the second would overwrite the first. So identity =
    owner + signature + begin line
Two methods can never share all three. The code checks this and
throws an error if it ever happens.

Signatures are NORMALIZED (real finding while testing):
    Map<String, Integer>      -> Map<String,Integer>
    Map< String ,  Integer >  -> Map<String,Integer>
JavaParser re-prints the type from the tree, dropping spaces and
comments. Good for us: reformatting code does not change identity.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 BIG IDEA 2 - OWNER LABELS AND THE STACK
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    Shop                 method directly in class Shop
    Shop.Size            "." = member type, a real importable name
    Shop#Local           "#" = local class inside a method (not importable)
    Shop#anonymous@48    the anonymous "new Runnable() {...}" on line 48
    Shop.Size#SMALL      the body of enum constant SMALL

How does the visitor know the owner? A STACK (a pile of plates):
    enter class Shop       push "Shop"          pile: [Shop]
    enter enum Size        push "Shop.Size"     pile: [Shop.Size, Shop]
      method weight()  -> owner = top of pile = "Shop.Size"
    leave enum Size        pop                  pile: [Shop]
    leave class Shop       pop                  pile: []

Java: Deque<String> owners = new ArrayDeque<>();
      owners.push(x)   put on top
      owners.peek()    look at top
      owners.pop()     take off top

Mutation check (real): removed owners.pop() -> labels went wrong ->
fixture test failed. Restored -> 64/64 pass.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 METHOD LINE RANGE RULES
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    /** Javadoc */      <- NOT part of the method (comments sit outside)
    @Deprecated         <- beginLine (annotations ARE part of it)
    String format(...) {
        // comment      <- inside, but not a code line
        return pattern;
    }                   <- endLine
    ncloc = 4  (annotation, signature, return, closing brace)

task() in the fixture has ncloc 11 because the local class and the
anonymous class are INSIDE its lines. Their own methods also get
their own records.

